shape theory.coherence.states : theory.coherence, theory.coherence.law1, theory.coherence.law2, theory.coherence.law3 {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definitions 5.10-5.12 (Coherence States).
//
// Coherent character (5.10): C is coherent under S when all
// relationships are realized. Contacts stable (Law 1), transformations
// conserve (Law 2), coupled shapes have resolved (Law 3).
//
// Decoherent character (5.11): C is decoherent under S when it
// contains shapes whose incompatible contact is unrealized: they are
// in contact through the emergence fractal, but mediated in a way
// that prevents the incompatibility from forcing resolution.
// Decoherence is potential coherence. When direct contact is forced,
// resolution produces coherence.
//
// Incoherent character (5.12): C is incoherent under S when S cannot
// handle C. Structural coherence fails. Leads to dissolution.
//
// The fundamental asymmetry: decoherence can persist indefinitely
// (stable unrealized relationship). But once contact forces collapse,
// coherence is the only destination.
//
// Derives from: theory.coherence, all three relational laws
  """
}
